from spell_evals_base import s

# ───────────── Rank 4 ─────────────
s('Fly', '000365', 'AAB', "Fly gives Cyrus or an ally a fly Speed for five minutes, and it becomes a studious spell at level 13, which adds a free Arcane Cascade. It solves most terrain problems and lets Cyrus engage flying enemies with Aspera instead of falling back on ranged cantrips. Flight also widens the angles available for Expansive and Sprinting Spellstrike, since Sprinting can use a fly Speed. The Druid and Cleric can cast it as well, so the party should agree who prepares it on a given day.")
s('Translocate', '000054', 'AAB', "Translocate teleports Cyrus up to 120 feet to a space he can see, which escapes grapples, crosses chasms and bypasses walls. At rank 5 it reaches a mile and can target a known location he can't see, making it a strong escape. It becomes a studious spell at level 13. In combat, Dimensional Assault covers most short teleports for one action, so Translocate's slot is best kept for escapes and exploration problems.")
s('Vision of Death', '403000', 'BCD', "Vision of Death deals heavy mental damage and imposes frightened 1 even on a successful save, so it always helps the party. It is one of the few Will payloads worth Cyrus's slots. Its weakness is the many undead and constructs immune to mental effects, and it relies on his spell DC, so it is best against living enemies with poor Will.")
s('Containment', '050300', 'BBD', "Containment encloses one creature in a force field. Used offensively, it isolates a dangerous enemy for the Reflex save's duration; used defensively, it protects a downed ally from follow-up attacks. The field also blocks the party's attacks, so it works best when the rest of the fight can be resolved while the contained creature waits.")
s('Force Rain', '400000', 'BCD', "The two-action version of Force Rain is a 10-foot force burst suitable for Expansive Spellstrike, and force damage is rarely resisted. The three-action version deals guaranteed damage without a save but can't be used through Spellstrike. It is a solid choice when Cyrus needs a dependable area spell against mixed enemies.")
s('Life-Draining Roots', '300200', 'CCD', "Life-Draining Roots is a 30-foot piercing line that gives Cyrus temporary Hit Points for each living creature it hits. Its line is short for Sprinting Spellstrike, and Lightning Bolt from a higher slot deals more damage over a longer line, so it rarely earns a place.")
s('Grasping Earth', '040000', 'BCD', "Grasping Earth grabs or restrains creatures in a 10-foot burst, and grabbed or restrained creatures are off-guard, which turns on Laughing Shadow's damage for Cyrus's next Strikes. Its damage only comes from sustaining it, which competes with his recharge actions. It is a good opening control spell against a group that wants to close on the party.")
s('Confusion', '040000', 'BCD', "Confusion stuns on a successful save and confuses on a failure, with the target saving at the end of each turn to end it. Confused enemies can attack their own allies, which is valuable against groups. Its reliance on Cyrus's spell DC makes it less dependable than control spells with stronger success effects.")
s('Unfettered Movement', '000330', 'CBC', "Unfettered Movement lets a creature ignore circumstance penalties to Speed and automatically escape most grapples for 10 minutes. It is best cast on the ally a known grappler is likely to target, which makes a scroll the natural way to carry it.")
s('Clairvoyance', '000004', 'CAB', "Clairvoyance creates an invisible eye at a location within 500 feet, even without line of sight. It takes a minute to cast, so it belongs to exploration and planning. It pairs well with the party's habit of resting between fights, since Cyrus can scout the next encounter before committing.")
s('Wall of Mirrors', '040003', 'ABD', "Wall of Mirrors raises a 50-foot wall for two actions that lasts 1 minute and can be dismissed early. Everything on each side is concealed from the other, so enemies firing or casting through it face a DC 5 flat check, and any creature that Strikes the wall takes mental damage. It is cheaper in actions than Wall of Stone and can be dropped when the party wants to advance, which suits a magus who needs his remaining action for a Stride or recharge. It doesn't block movement or line of effect, so it controls ranged pressure rather than splitting a fight, and its sections can be broken by a determined melee enemy. As a stave spell it gives Cyrus a once-a-day battlefield tool without spending a slot.")

# ───────────── Rank 5 ─────────────
s('Weight of the World', '354000', 'SBD', "Weight of the World stuns the target even on a successful save and adds dazzled, so it always costs the enemy at least one action. On a failure, stunned 2 removes two actions from a boss's next turn. Delivered through Spellstrike alongside Aspera's damage, it is the best Fortitude payload at rank 5 and a priority for Cyrus's top slots from level 9.")
s('Wall of Stone', '060043', 'SAC', "Wall of Stone takes three actions to raise up to 120 feet of stone wall, which can split an encounter in half, block reinforcements or create a bridge or staircase. It is the strongest control spell Cyrus can cast at this rank. It cannot be delivered through Spellstrike, so it costs a full turn, which is justified when it removes half the enemies from the next few rounds.")
s('Glacial Skewer', '530040', 'ACD', "Glacial Skewer deals heavy cold and piercing damage on Aspera's attack roll and pushes the target. If the push drives it into a Large or larger obstacle, it is immobilised for up to a minute. Cyrus should position so a wall or pillar is behind the target before using it, and pair it with Sure Strike when the fight depends on the hit.")
s('Blazing Fissure', '432000', 'ACD', "Blazing Fissure is a 120-foot line where every creature on solid ground that fails its save falls prone. With Sprinting Spellstrike, Cyrus can run the length of the line and knock every enemy along his path prone before he Strikes, leaving them off-guard for Laughing Shadow's damage and for his allies. It is the strongest line spell for setting up the party at this rank.")
s('Tornadic Gale', '430040', 'ACD', "Tornadic Gale first pulls Medium or smaller creatures adjacent to the line into it, then damages everything in the line. With Expansive and Sprinting Spellstrike, the line follows Cyrus's movement, so it gathers enemies from beside his route as well as those directly in it. It is a strong choice when enemies are spread out near a corridor or approach route.")
s('Howling Blizzard', '420000', 'BCD', "The two-action version of Howling Blizzard is a 60-foot cone suitable for Expansive Spellstrike, and it leaves difficult terrain until Cyrus's next turn. The three-action burst version reaches farther but can't be used through Spellstrike. It is a solid cold area option when the cone can be aimed away from the party.")
s('Impaling Spike', '340000', 'BCD', "Impaling Spike immobilises a target that fails its save and leaves it off-guard on a critical failure. The spike is made of cold iron, which matters against fey and demons, both common in the Forgotten Realms. It is a good single-target control payload when a creature needs to be pinned in place.")
s('Shadow Siphon', '000400', 'CCD', "Shadow Siphon is a legacy reaction that can halve the damage of an enemy spell for every creature it affects. It is valuable against enemy blasters, but it competes with Reactive Strike for Cyrus's reaction and depends on a counteract check.")
s('Corrosive Muck', '340000', 'BCD', "Corrosive Muck creates two pools of greater difficult terrain that damage creatures entering or starting their turn in them. It is best cast normally to close off approach routes or protect the party's casters.")
s('Banishment', '050000', 'CCD', "Banishment sends an extraplanar creature back to its home plane. That matters against the devils and demons the Forgotten Realms often features, but the incapacitation trait limits it against powerful fiends, which are the ones the party most needs removed.")
s('Space Fold Gate', '000054', 'CBD', "Space Fold Gate links two squares up to 200 feet apart for a minute, so the whole party can cross a gap or reach an objective. Enemies can use the gate as well, so its placement needs thought.")
s('Magic Passage', '000004', 'CAD', "Magic Passage opens a tunnel through up to 10 feet of stone, wood or plaster for an hour. Any metal in the wall blocks it. A scroll is the sensible choice for a raid on a fortified site.")
s('Scouting Eye', '000004', 'CBC', "Scouting Eye creates a mobile invisible eye that can follow a route. It is more flexible than Clairvoyance when there is somewhere specific to scout.")
s('Sending', '000004', 'CAC', "Sending delivers a 25-word message to a creature Cyrus knows well anywhere on the same planet, with a reply. A scroll covers the occasional need to reach a patron or ally far away.")

# ───────────── Rank 6 ─────────────
s('Disintegrate', '600000', 'ABD', "Disintegrate deals 12d10 untyped damage on Aspera's attack roll, but the target still gets a basic Fortitude save, and a critical hit only worsens that save by one degree. Against a level-14 boss at level 12, with Sure Strike, it averages about 25 spell damage against a moderate Fortitude save, where Blood Feast heightened to rank 6 averages about 37 with no save; it only pulls level against low Fortitude. Its strengths are the ceiling, since a critical hit against a failed save doubles to around 130 damage, enemies whose Fortitude has been lowered by Blister Bomb or Eagle's Cry, and its utility: it destroys a wall of force or a 10-foot cube of matter outright, and a creature it reduces to 0 Hit Points is left as dust.")
s('Chain Lightning', '400000', 'BCD', "Chain Lightning only affects one target through Spellstrike, so it should be cast normally. The chain ends if any target critically succeeds, which happens more often against Cyrus's spell DC than a full caster's.")
s('Living Thunderbolt', '300450', 'ACD', "Living Thunderbolt gives Cyrus a 60-foot fly Speed for a minute, resistance to electricity, automatic escapes from most grabs and restraints, and lets him move through creatures, dealing electricity damage to each one once per round. It is a polymorph spell but not a battle form, so he keeps Aspera and casts normally. Its value is in combination with Sprinting Spellstrike from level 12: the Sprinting movement can be flown, so a line spell through a group also adds Living Thunderbolt's damage to every creature on the path. On its own it is a strong mobility buff for a minute-long fight. The cost is two actions on a turn with no Spellstrike, so it is best cast before contact or on a turn spent closing distance.")
s('Wall of Force', '050000', 'ABD', "Wall of Force creates an invisible wall with Hardness 30 that lasts a minute. It blocks physical effects and incorporeal creatures, making it one of the strongest ways to divide a fight. It costs three actions and can't be used through Spellstrike.")
s('Silver Spear', '500000', 'ACD', "Silver Spear deals 12d6 piercing damage on Aspera's attack roll, with an extra 12d6 against fiends and a teleport lock on a critical hit. The spear is silver, which matters against devils.")
s('Petrify', '040000', 'BCD', "Petrify slows the target even on a successful save. On a failure, the target risks permanent petrification over several turns, though each further save has the incapacitation trait.")
s('Cast into Time', '330000', 'CCD', "Cast into Time removes every creature in the cone until the end of Cyrus's turn, so he can't follow up on them that turn. Its main value is the damage they take when they return.")
s('Unexpected Transposition', '000430', 'BCD', "Unexpected Transposition is a reaction that swaps Cyrus with another creature so an attack hits them instead. Swapping with an enemy gives the best result, but the reaction competes with Reactive Strike.")
s('Collective Transposition', '020050', 'BBD', "Collective Transposition teleports two or more creatures within 30 feet. It can move allies into flanking positions or move an enemy away from a downed ally.")
s('Truesight', '000005', 'CAC', "Truesight lets Cyrus see through illusions and shapechangers for 10 minutes. A scroll suits an infiltration or a court intrigue where impostors are likely.")
s('Mislead', '000433', 'BBD', "Mislead makes Cyrus invisible and creates an illusory duplicate that he directs. It suits deception and repositioning, but sustaining it costs an action each turn.")
s('Teleport', '000005', 'CAC', "Teleport moves the party up to 100 miles after a 10-minute cast. It is an expedition tool rather than a combat spell.")

# ───────────── Rank 7 ─────────────
s('True Target', '000600', 'SBC', "True Target costs one action and lets Cyrus and up to three allies roll their first attack against the designated creature twice, ignoring concealment. Cyrus can cast it and Spellstrike on the same turn. It is most effective when the party's attackers act before the target does, so the timing in initiative matters.")
s('Frigid Flurry', '500050', 'SCD', "Frigid Flurry is one of the best line payloads Cyrus can learn. It damages only foes, so it can be sent through a melee that includes the party, and after the Strike and the damage resolve, the wind carries Cyrus to the far end of the line while he is immune to almost everything. Through Expansive Spellstrike that means he hits a whole file of enemies and ends well away from them; with Sprinting Spellstrike the line follows his path, so he can cut through a group, Strike, and be carried on to the end of the line. The weakness is fire, and the carry ends his position at the line's far end, which can put him out of reach of the next target or away from the party's healer.")
s('Beheading Buzz Saw', '400000', 'BCD', "Beheading Buzz Saw is a 60-foot line with heavy persistent bleed and a chance of decapitation on a critical failure. A successful save means no damage at all, which is a real risk against Cyrus's spell DC.")
s('Eclipse Burst', '400000', 'CCD', "Eclipse Burst is a 60-foot burst that's too large for Expansive Spellstrike, so it should be cast normally from a distance. The Druid's spells cover large areas well, so Cyrus rarely needs it.")
s('Telekinetic Bombardment', '440000', 'ACD', "Telekinetic Bombardment knocks prone on a failure and stuns on a critical failure, and it leaves difficult terrain behind. It can be placed anywhere within 500 feet, including as a line that doesn't start from Cyrus, which gives it unusual flexibility.")
s('Comet Charge', '500050', 'ACD', "Comet Charge is a large single-target payload with a choice of four damage types, which makes it a reliable way to hit a known weakness. Through Spellstrike it uses Aspera's attack roll, which is higher than his spell attack, and the flight happens after the Strike resolves, which pulls Cyrus adjacent to the target and gives up his reach advantage. Cast normally it is a strong way to reach an isolated enemy up to 120 feet away without triggering reactions, but it then uses his weaker spell attack. It competes with save spells of the same rank that still do something on a miss, so it is best when the target's AC is clearly its weakest defence.")
s('Defy the Gods', '005000', 'BCD', "Defy the Gods drains and stupefies the target even on a successful save. It weakens an enemy caster and is especially effective against divine servants.")
s('Spell Riposte', '000403', 'BCD', "Spell Riposte reflects a targeted spell back at its caster if Cyrus counteracts it. It should be prepared for a known fight against a caster.")
s('Contingency', '000403', 'BBC', "Contingency sets up a spell such as Translocate, Fly or Invisibility to trigger automatically when Cyrus is in trouble. It takes 10 minutes and should be cast during the morning's preparations.")

# ───────────── Rank 8 ─────────────
s('Arctic Rift', '540000', 'ACD', "Arctic Rift is a 120-foot Fortitude line, giving Cyrus a Sprinting Spellstrike payload for enemies with strong Reflex. A failure slows the target, and a critical failure encases it in ice.")
s('Disappearance', '000656', 'SAC', "Disappearance makes Cyrus invisible to every precise sense for 10 minutes, even while he attacks. Every Strike he makes is against an off-guard target, which turns on Laughing Shadow's damage every turn.")
s('Quandary', '060000', 'ACD', "Quandary has no initial save, so the target is removed from the fight until it solves the puzzle against Cyrus's spell DC. Sustaining it costs one action each turn, which is a small price for removing a boss from several rounds.")
s('Roar of Freedom', '403400', 'ACD', "Roar of Freedom costs one action, damages enemies within 30 feet and grants allies 15 temporary Hit Points. It fits alongside a Spellstrike on the same turn, which makes it one of the most action-efficient spells he will have.")
s('Desiccate', '500000', 'BCD', "Desiccate damages any number of living creatures within 500 feet with a basic Fortitude save. It should be cast normally to keep its selectivity.")
s('Uncontrollable Dance', '054000', 'ACD', "Uncontrollable Dance leaves the target off-guard and unable to use reactions for three rounds even on a successful save. It is a touch spell, so Spellstrike delivers it at reach. The incapacitation trait limits it against higher-level enemies.")
s('Falling Sky', '050000', 'ACD', "Falling Sky knocks every creature in the cylinder prone even on a successful save, and flying creatures crash to the ground. A failure also stuns. It has the incapacitation trait.")

# ───────────── Rank 9 ─────────────
s('Foresight', '000603', 'SAC', "Foresight lets Cyrus reroll a priority ally's saves, or force enemies to reroll attacks against that ally, for an hour. With one or two fights a day, it covers the most important fight. Cast it on the Champion or whoever the boss will target.")
s('Remake Physiology', '046030', 'SCD', "Remake Physiology imposes clumsy, drained, enfeebled, stupefied and dazzled and a −20-foot Speed penalty, even for a round on a successful save. It is a touch spell, so Spellstrike delivers it at reach.")
s('Falling Stars', '520000', 'BCD', "Falling Stars creates four 40-foot bursts within 500 feet. It should be cast normally on an open battlefield.")
s('Phantasmagoria', '440000', 'BCD', "Phantasmagoria damages any number of creatures and confuses those that fail, and a successful save still prevents their reactions.")
s('Dimensional Excision', '500000', 'ACD', "Dimensional Excision deals basic Will damage without the mental trait, with a −4 penalty for creatures away from their home plane. It is strong against extraplanar bosses.")
s('Implosion', '400000', 'BCD', "Implosion deals 75 damage to one target, then a new target each time it is sustained. Sustaining it competes with Cyrus's recharge actions.")
s('Massacre', '500000', 'BCD', "Massacre kills creatures of level 17 or lower that fail their save in a 60-foot line. If nothing dies, it backfires on Cyrus.")
